-**Labels come from folders:** files under `phish/` are phishing, files under `legit/` are legitimate. To override one file, add `data/samples/labels.csv`:
+**Labels come from folders:** files under `phish/` are phishing, files under `legit/` are legitimate. To override one file, add `data/samples/labels.csv`. Prefer a root-relative `path` so files with the same basename cannot collide:
 
 ```
-filename,label
-sample-9.eml,legit
+path,label
+phish/sample-9.eml,legit
 ```
+
+The older `filename,label` format remains supported when that filename is unique in the dataset:
+
+```
+filename,label
+sample-9.eml,legit
+```
+
+If more than one candidate has that basename, the filename-only override is ignored and a warning is printed. Use `path,label` to target one file. If both columns contain values on a row, `path` takes priority.
+
+### Campaign-aware dev/test split and dataset manifest
+
+Add an optional `data/samples/manifest.csv` to keep related messages in the same split and record provenance:
+
+```csv
+path,group_id,dataset,license,reference,collection_date
+phish/0001.eml,phishing-pot:campaign-17,Phishing Pot,CC-BY-SA-4.0,https://example.org/dataset,2026-01-01
+phish/0002.eml,phishing-pot:campaign-17,Phishing Pot,CC-BY-SA-4.0,https://example.org/dataset,2026-01-01
+legit/modern/0001.eml,modern-mail:batch-1,Your dataset,private,local,2026-01-01
+```
+
+- `path` is relative to the evaluation root and uses `/` separators. It must not be absolute or contain `.` or `..` path components.
+- `group_id` is optional. Samples with the same non-empty ID always go to the same 80/20 split. Use stable, globally distinct IDs; prefix them with the dataset name when needed (for example, `phishing-pot:campaign-17`).
+- `dataset`, `license`, `reference` and `collection_date` are optional provenance fields. The date should use `YYYY-MM-DD` when known.
+- Samples without a `group_id` keep the original individual-email SHA-256 split. No campaign inference is performed from sender, domain or subject.
+- Every manifest path must match an evaluation sample (or be inside a folder excluded by `--skip-dir`). A malformed or unmatched manifest stops evaluation rather than silently reverting to the sample-level split. `--from-history` does not use this manifest.
+
+This grouping is only as complete as the IDs you provide. It does not automatically detect near-duplicates or discover campaign relationships.
